From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Name AVP 303 as ETSI ES 283 034 does

ETSI ES 283 034 V2.2.0 clause 7.3.4 defines AVP 303 (vendor ETSI) as
Initial-Gate-Setting-Description, and table 10 and the User-Data-Answer
and Push-Notification-Request ABNFs (clauses 7.1.2, 7.1.3) name it so.

Renaming an AVP renames its display filter field
(diameter.Initial-Gate-Setting becomes
diameter.Initial-Gate-Setting-Description), so saved filters and profiles
using the old name need updating.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
index a48da2b..6ab4d95 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
 	<avp name="Logical-Access-ID" code="302" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
 		<type type-name="OctetString"/>
 	</avp>
-	<avp name="Initial-Gate-Setting" code="303" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
+	<avp name="Initial-Gate-Setting-Description" code="303" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
 		<grouped>
 			<gavp name="NAS-Filter-Rule"/>
 			<gavp name="Maximum-Allowed-Bandwidth-UL"/>
